-- Study plans: move the issued copies to the updated templates (Jira SKD-42, SKD-43).
--
-- A student's copy of a plan is frozen when it is issued, and the templates were
-- rewritten after the first issue (the school's updated sheets: 9 modules instead of 8,
-- GitHub Actions instead of Jenkins, new homeworks). This migration changes the data
-- only, no schema: every issued plan becomes a copy of the current template of its track.
--
-- How an old item finds its new place: each item has a key, the chain of
-- «kind:title#n» of its ancestors and itself (n counts equal siblings). _plan_map says which
-- key of the updated template an old key becomes: by title inside the same topic, a
-- homework follows its topic, a homework sub-task is found by its number. The map holds the keys of
-- every template version that was ever issued; it was built from git (5104eb4, 2115292,
-- 751ae49) and the current files by a one-off script, the list is in the pull request.
--   · a matched item keeps its id, tick, doneAt and note; only its title, place and link change;
--   · an item of the updated template that nothing matched is added, not done;
--   · an old item that nothing matched is deleted — but only if it has no tick and no note;
--   · Plan rows are neither added nor deleted.
-- The last steps are the guard: the migration fails (and changes nothing) if an old item with a
-- tick or a note would be lost, or if any plan of these tracks differs from its template after
-- the move.

BEGIN;

CREATE TEMP TABLE _plan_new (
  track TEXT NOT NULL, key TEXT NOT NULL, parent_key TEXT NOT NULL, kind TEXT NOT NULL,
  title TEXT NOT NULL, position INTEGER NOT NULL, material_url TEXT, PRIMARY KEY (track, key)
);
